Note: Editor's Note: Insert the following subclause between 24.3.7.5 Concept `indirectly_comparable` [alg.req.ind.cmp] and 24.3.7.6 Concept `permutable` [alg.req.permutable]

## 24.3.7.� Concept `searchable` [alg.req.searchable] ## {#alg.req.searchable}

1. The `searchable` concept specifies the requirements of algorithms that interact with searchers (22.10.18 [func.search]) to search for a sequence in another sequence.

```cpp
template<class Searcher, class I, class S, class P = identity>
  concept searchable =
    movable<Searcher> &&
    invocable<const Searcher&, I, S, P> &&
    ranges::forward_range<invoke_result_t<const Searcher&, I, S, P>>
```

