# Wording for Optional Additional Changes # {#wording-optional}

Note: The wording below is for the standalone additional breaking change to `std::search`.

## 26.6.15 Search [alg.search] ## {#alg.search-optional}

Modify paragraph 11-12 as indicated:

```cpp
template<class ForwardIterator, class Searcher>
  constexpr ForwardIterator
    search(ForwardIterator first, ForwardIterator last, const Searcher& searcher);
```

11. *Effects*: Equivalent to: <del>`return searcher(first, last).first;`</del><ins>`return std::get<0>(searcher(first, last));`</ins>
12. *Remarks*: `Searcher` need not meet the *Cpp17CopyConstructible* requirements.

# Poll Results # {#poll-results}
## SG9 Review, Brno (2026-06) ## {#sg9-review-brno}

**Poll 1**: We want both `operator()(begin, end)` and `operator()(range)` on the standardized searchers.

<table>
    <thead><tr><td>Strongly Favor</td><td>Favor</td><td>Neutral</td><td>Against</td><td>Strongly Against</td></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody>
</table>

- **Outcome**: No consensus.

**Poll 2**: We want only `operator()(begin, end)` on the standardized searchers.

<table>
    <thead><tr><td>Strongly Favor</td><td>Favor</td><td>Neutral</td><td>Against</td><td>Strongly Against</td></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody>
</table>

- **Outcome**: Consensus in favor.

**Poll 3**: We want only `operator()(range)` on the standardized searchers.

<table>
    <thead><tr><td>Strongly Favor</td><td>Favor</td><td>Neutral</td><td>Against</td><td>Strongly Against</td></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>5</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody>
</table>

- **Outcome**: Consensus against.

